hadiths[4]{hadithnumber,text}:
"15635","Ubaydah ibn Humayd narrated to us, he said: Yazid ibn Abi Ziyad narrated to me, from Mujahid, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Safwan, he said: I saw the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, between the Stone and the Door, placing his face upon the House."
"15636","Jarir narrated to us, from Yazid ibn Abi Ziyad, from Mujahid, he said: There was a man among the Emigrants called Abd al-Rahman ibn Safwan, and he had fine valor in Islam, and he was a friend of al-Abbas. When it was the day of the conquest of Makkah, he came with his father to the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and said: O Messenger of Allah, pledge him to emigration. But he refused and said: There is no emigration. So he went to al-Abbas while he was at the water supply, and said: O Abu al-Fadl, I came to the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, with my father to pledge him to emigration, but he refused. He said: So al-Abbas stood with him with no cloak on him, and said: O Messenger of Allah, you know what is between me and So-and-so, and he came to you with his father to pledge him to emigration, but you refused. So the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: There is no emigration. Al-Abbas said: I adjure you to pledge him. He said: So the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, stretched his hand. He said: He said: Bring, I have fulfilled the oath of my uncle, and there is no emigration."
"15637","Ahmad ibn al-Hajjaj narrated to us, Jarir ibn Abd al-Hamid narrated to us, from Yazid ibn Abi Ziyad, from Mujahid, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Safwan, he said: I saw the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, clinging to the Door between the Stone and the Door, and I saw the people clinging to the House with the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him."
"15638","Ahmad ibn al-Hajjaj narrated to us, Jarir informed us, from Yazid ibn Abi Ziyad, from Mujahid, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Safwan, he said: When the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, conquered Makkah, I said: I will wear my clothes, and my house was on the road, so I will see what the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, does. So I went, and I found the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, had come out of the Kabah, and his Companions had touched the House from the Door to the Hatim, and had placed their cheeks upon the House, and the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, was among them. So I said to Umar: How did the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, do when he entered the Kabah. He said: He prayed two rakahs."
